// A read the source already decides cannot succeed.
//
// `xs` is written out as three elements and `99` is written out as the index,
// so nothing has to run for this to be wrong. The array's type is `[(1|2|3)]`
// and carries no length — the length comes from the literal the binding was
// given, and it is read for this diagnostic and for nothing else.
//
// The rule is narrow on purpose. An aliased array (`let ys = xs;`), an array a
// function returned, an array written with a spread, and an index that is only
// *typed* as one integer are all refused by name: they say nothing here and
// still trap at run time.

open @import "blot:prelude" ()

let xs = [1, 2, 3]
return @array.get xs 99
